{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISION (operator-approved, 2026-08-30): **Option A — detect-and-signal only.**\n\nFix scope for THIS ticket is narrowed to closing the SILENT-failure defect, NOT full auto-apply:\n- Enumerate `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` (and any other edge input) in an autodeploy detect manifest so a merged edge change is DETECTED.\n- On a detected edge delta, raise the `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` detect-and-signal treatment that `CONFIG_PATHS` already gets (bug 1630 precedent) — an operator then applies it. Do NOT implement unattended render/`nginx -t`/reload here.\n- Blast radius: never touch the `gerrit` container; this change adds a manifest entry + a signal path + tests only. No box mutation.\n\nRationale + standing intent: ADR 0079 (story 8903) deliberately scoped v1 auto-apply to the review-bot container and made Gerrit config DETECT-ONLY, explicitly deferring \"config auto-apply\" to v2 because auto-applying config to a box hosting a live fail-closed submit gate is high-risk. The nginx edge falls in that same deferred bucket; the genuine defect here is that it fell through BOTH categories and gets no signal at all. Option A restores it to parity with CONFIG_PATHS without crossing the deferred v1->v2 boundary. OSS precedent: Argo CD keeps drift DETECTION always-on but auto-sync opt-in; Terraform separates plan from apply.\n\nThe full unattended auto-apply (Option B) is captured as idea epic **sprucing-wise-dikkops (6d60-2d0c-6ff7-444b)** — needs its own design + ADR before promotion.\n\nAC update for Option A: AC2 collapses to the \"signalled via AUTODEPLOY_ERROR\" branch (drop the \"or applied\" alternative). AC \"malformed conf fails nginx -t and is rolled back\" moves to the Option B epic. The \"a61d unblocked / verified live at the edge\" AC is satisfied by a SEPARATE operator deploy after this lands (a shared-box mutation requiring approval), not by this change.\n\nDispatching a background /rebar-debug agent to implement under this narrowed scope."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788110203745730394,"uuid":"56b46f5f-c24f-46e8-9299-1c33bb21c67c"}